WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.602
On this slide, we are focusing on create a list.

00:00:03.602 --> 00:00:08.472
Start with the meaning of the idea before worrying about the exact syntax.

00:00:08.472 --> 00:00:14.622
Ask what information is going in, what Python is doing with it, and what result should come out.

00:00:14.622 --> 00:00:17.872
A list is an ordered collection that can change.

00:00:17.872 --> 00:00:24.742
It is useful when values may be added, removed, replaced, sorted, or processed over time.

00:00:24.742 --> 00:00:27.882
Before clicking Run, predict the output.

00:00:27.882 --> 00:00:34.032
Then run the cell, inspect the result, and change one value or condition at a time.

00:00:34.032 --> 00:00:37.372
Rerun it and explain why the output changed.

00:00:37.372 --> 00:00:42.386
The goal is to understand the relationship between input, process, and output.
